            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg: Is it a question of just how you phrase it, Mr. Olson? Is there any scope for state attorney general imposition of state law remedies against a deceptive practice involving advertising cigarettes?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souter, justice Souter: Mr. Olson, doesn't your answer in effect, in practical terms, exclude the possibility of inserts like that? I mean, what else would they be addressing except smoking and health?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, justice Kennedy: Suppose a new drug is found for the treatment of a condition, glaucoma\u2014hypothetical\u2014and the evidence is stunningly clear that smoking with this new drug causes a severe allergic reaction. Does the cigarette manufacturer have any duty to disclose this on the label or in promotions?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer: In Cipollone, does the statute not pre\u2011empt State law where it is based on a prohibition of making a false statement of material fact?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Stevens, justice Stevens: Is a State requirement prohibiting false statements about smoking and health a requirement based on smoking and health?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souter, justice Souter: Isn't the problem that Congress was equally clear, or has at least been assumed to be equally clear, in a contrary line of reasoning that holds against you? That line of reasoning is that the FTC can regulate advertising and deception that relate to smoking and health."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg: Could a state attorney general, under your authority to check against false and deceptive advertising, say no cigarette company can advertise low or light in this State?"
      }
    ],
